  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Application Stack**\n\nI am currently solidifying the application\'s technological backbone. I\'ve confirmed React with Vite, Tailwind v4, and `lucide-react` for icons. I\'m also including `motion/react` for animations and `@google/genai` is there too. My focus is on ensuring these components integrate seamlessly.\n\n\n**Assessing API Dependencies**\n\nI\'m now reconsidering the Gemini API implementation. I\'m leaning toward a client-side approach, unless there\'s a strong justification for a server-side Gemini integration. The core idea is a personal gamer dashboard pulling data from Steam, Discord, Riot, Minecraft, and FVTT, using a visual style with neon purple/blue tones and doodle-like background elements.\n\n\n**Refining the Neon Visuals**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual design, leaning towards generating custom glowing neon elements directly in React using SVG and `lucide-react`. This approach offers complete interactive control and pristine styling. I\'ve also identified the need to refine the application name in `metadata.json` based on the user\'s initial request, ensuring it\'s descriptive and literal. I\'ll read about `image-generation` but I don\'t strictly need it.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will start by reviewing the project structure and editing `metadata.json` to properly configure the application metadata with an appropriate title and description reflecting your request. Then, I will design a gorgeous gaming information dashboard styled with neon-purple-and-blue accents, custom glowing SVG controllers and game doodles, and separate navigation tabs for \"About me\", \"Video games\", and \"TTRPG\". Let\'s view the `metadata.json` and package configurations."
